message.content:
Use CSS `:hover` on the `span` itself. The `:hover` pseudo-class applies when the pointer is over an element, and it works on all elements, not just links.[6][7]

```html
<span class="my-span">Hover me</span>
```

```css
.my-span {
  color: black;
}

.my-span:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If the color does not change, another rule may be overriding it. In that case, make the hover selector more specific or remove the conflicting inline style, since inline styling can override stylesheet rules.[1][6]

```css
.my-span:hover {
  color: red !important;
}
```

If you want, I can also show how to change the color with a smooth transition or how to do it for only part of the text inside a larger element.

